  "title": "Federal Government Fiscal-Year-Close Delta — September 26–30, 2026",
  "question": "What materially changed across official U.S. federal, committee and adjacent-institution sources after the September 25 close through the September 30 post-noon replay, and what did fiscal-year close actually prove?",
  "bluf": "The September 30 surge is real but still procedure-, control- and implementation-heavy. Deeper site review added a sanctions-list action, a live student-loan default portal and Amtrak's Airo passenger-service launch; committee review found an FSOC budget vote, prediction-market information requests and a charter/meeting-notice batch; adjacent review found Farm Credit issuance and settlement, New York Fed operations and clearing-governance changes. The post-noon replay added SEC proposals, FSA's lagged official cohort-default-rate release, a resolved CFTC judgment and a noon New York Fed operation. None proves a government-wide final-day payment sweep, and later-day high-velocity surfaces remain provisional.",
